# International > Date Format (dialog 15): short date DMY with "-" and the day's leading zero, long
# date order DMY with "ddd", OK, then OK in International (focus is back on Change..., so tab to
# OK) - WIN.INI [intl] is written. Same keys as arch311-ref/scn/intl-date.scn after opening. Run as
# intl.w16 (ARCH311_PRISTINE_INI=1, ARCH311_CLOCK="2026-10-08 09:30:24", applet International).
# regress: ARCH311_PRISTINE_INI=1 ARCH311_CLOCK="2026-10-08 09:30:24" sh tools/run-cp-test.sh "$TEST" "$OUT" International
# compare: intl-date/02.png 01-open.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: intl-date/03.png 02-date.png active ignore 317 231 324 248
# compare: intl-date/04.png 03-short.png active ignore 317 231 324 248
# compare: intl-date/05.png 04-long-dmy.png active ignore 317 231 324 248
# compare: intl-date/06.png 05-ddd.png active ignore 317 231 324 248
# compare: intl-date/07.png 06-samples.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# ini: WIN.INI intl iDate=1
# ini: WIN.INI intl sDate=-
# ini: WIN.INI intl sShortDate=dd-M-yy
# ini: WIN.INI intl sLongDate=ddd', 'dd' 'MMMM', 'yyyy
# ini: WIN.INI intl sCountry=United States
sleep 900
shot shots/01-open.png
key tab
key tab
key tab
key tab
key tab
key enter
sleep 600
shot shots/02-date.png
key right
key tab
type -
key tab
key space
sleep 300
shot shots/03-short.png
key tab
key tab
key tab
key right
sleep 300
shot shots/04-long-dmy.png
key tab
key up
sleep 300
shot shots/05-ddd.png
key enter
sleep 500
shot shots/06-samples.png
key tab
key tab
key tab
key tab
key enter
sleep 400
quit
